/-! # The degree-two derivation attached to a principal square-zero extension

Let `q : R' → R` be a surjection of commutative rings whose kernel is generated by a single
element `f` of square zero, and let `A` be a nonnegatively graded `R`-algebra with a differential
`d` lowering degrees by one. Suppose `(A, d)` lifts across `q`: there is a graded `R'`-algebra
`B` with a degree-lowering operator `D` obeying the signed Leibniz rule, a grading-preserving
surjection `π : B → A` whose kernel is `f · B` and which intertwines `D` with `d`, and a
comparison map `κ : ker π → A/IA` sending `f · b` to the class of `π b`, where `I ⊆ R` is the
image under `q` of the annihilator of `f`.

The operator `D` need not be square-zero — that failure is the whole point. What is true is that
`π` sends `D (D b)` to `d (d (π b)) = 0`, so `D ∘ D` takes values in `ker π = f · B`, and
`κ ∘ D ∘ D` descends along `π` to an `R`-linear operator `θ` on `A/IA`. Because the two Koszul
signs in the Leibniz rule cancel, `D ∘ D` is an *unsigned* derivation, and `θ` is therefore a
derivation of degree `-2` on `A/IA` vanishing in degrees zero and one.

This file proves that implication, in two formulations, for a given lift; it is one half of
[Stacks, Tag 09PS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09PS). The construction of the lift
`(B, D)` is the other half, in
`StacksFrontier.RingTheory.DividedPowers.TateResolution.SquareZeroLift`.

## Main definitions

* `DividedPowers.TateResolution.squareZeroAnnihilator` — the ideal `I` of `R`, the image under
  `q` of the annihilator of the square-zero generator.
* `DividedPowers.TateResolution.squareZeroAnnihilatorSMul` — the submodule `I · A` of `A`.
* `DividedPowers.TateResolution.IsSquareZeroLift` — the hypotheses on `(B, ℬ, π, D, κ)` making
  it a lift of `(A, 𝒜, d)` across `q`, as a predicate over explicit data.
* `DividedPowers.TateResolution.IsSquareZeroLift.derivation` — the resulting operator `θ`.
* `DividedPowers.TateResolution.IsDividedPowerSquareZeroLift` — such a lift which moreover
  carries divided powers compatible with `π` and with `D`.

## Main results

* `DividedPowers.TateResolution.IsSquareZeroLift.derivation_apply` says that `θ` is `κ ∘ D ∘ D`.
  This determines `θ`, which the derivation properties alone do not: the zero map has all of
  them.
* `DividedPowers.TateResolution.IsSquareZeroLift.derivation_leibniz`,
  `DividedPowers.TateResolution.IsSquareZeroLift.derivation_mem_grade`,
  `DividedPowers.TateResolution.IsSquareZeroLift.derivation_eq_zero_of_mem_grade_zero` and
  `DividedPowers.TateResolution.IsSquareZeroLift.derivation_eq_zero_of_mem_grade_one` are the
  four properties of a derivation of degree `-2`.
* `DividedPowers.TateResolution.IsSquareZeroLift.D_comp_D_mul` says that `D ∘ D` is an unsigned
  derivation, and `DividedPowers.TateResolution.IsSquareZeroLift.map_D_comp_D` that it lands in
  the kernel of the lift.
* `DividedPowers.TateResolution.IsSquareZeroLift.exists_homogeneous_preimage` says that a
  degree-preserving surjection between graded objects is surjective in each degree.
* `DividedPowers.TateResolution.exists_derivation_of_differentialLift` is the same descent in
  existential form, over the raw data of a lift and with the comparison map constructed rather
  than supplied. What makes that construction well defined is that an element of `B` killed by
  `f` lies in `ann (f) • ⊤`; that conclusion, rather than freeness itself, is the form in which
  the hypothesis is taken, and
  `DividedPowers.TateResolution.mem_annihilator_smul_top_of_smul_eq_zero` is how a free `B`
  supplies it.
* `DividedPowers.TateResolution.exists_addMonoidHom_comp_of_surjective` says that an additive map
  killing the kernel of a surjective additive map factors through it, and
  `DividedPowers.TateResolution.coe_decompose_addMonoidHom` that an additive map carrying each
  homogeneous piece into the piece of the same degree commutes with taking homogeneous
  components.
* `DividedPowers.TateResolution.restrictScalars_map_algebraMap` identifies the ideal of `A`
  generated by a central scalar ideal `I` with the `R`-submodule `I · A`, so that the
  derivation's target may be described either way.

## Implementation notes

The comparison map `κ` is taken as data together with its defining equation on `f · b`, rather
than constructed from `π` and `D`. Constructing it would require identifying the annihilator of
`f` in `B` with `ann(f) · B`, hence freeness of `B` over `R'`, and the argument does not
need that: the equation `κ (f · b) = [π b]` already determines `κ` on all of `ker π`, since
every element of the kernel is of that form, and it already forces `κ` to be `q`-semilinear.
The hypotheses on `(B, ℬ, π, D, κ)` are therefore kept as a predicate over explicit data instead
of a bundled existential, so that each of them can be cited individually.

Strict graded commutativity of `ℬ`, its divided powers, and the divided-power Leibniz rule for
`D` play no role in reading the derivation off a lift: they are needed to *construct* one. They
are consequently absent from `IsSquareZeroLift` and collected in
`IsDividedPowerSquareZeroLift`, which extends it; that is the form the Gulliksen argument of
Tag 09PU runs on.

`exists_derivation_of_differentialLift` spells the lift out field by field instead of bundling
it, assumes that an element of `B` killed by `f` lies in `ann (f) • ⊤`, and constructs `κ`
rather than receiving it; in exchange its conclusion mentions no divided powers. Neither
formulation subsumes the other, so both are kept.

The two facts about `D ∘ D` that drive both proofs are consequences of the signed Leibniz rule
for `D` and neither mentions a sign. First, `D ∘ D` is an *unsigned* derivation: on homogeneous
`b` of degree `i` the two cross terms of the double Leibniz expansion carry the coefficients
`(-1) ^ (i - 1)` and `(-1) ^ i`, which cancel, so `D (D (b * c)) = D (D b) * c + b * D (D c)`
with no sign at all, and both sides are then additive in each argument, which is what lets the
identity be extended off the homogeneous elements. Second, `π ∘ D ∘ D = d ∘ d ∘ π = 0`, so
`D ∘ D` lands in the kernel of `π`.

A graded form of surjectivity of `π` is not assumed by either formulation: it follows from plain
surjectivity together with `π` being grading preserving, by commuting `π` with the homogeneous
component maps (`IsSquareZeroLift.exists_homogeneous_preimage` for the bundled formulation,
`coe_decompose_addMonoidHom` for the unbundled one). The same lemma, applied to multiplication
by `f` — which is homogeneous of degree zero — is what lets the chosen preimage under
multiplication by `f` be taken homogeneous, which is what the degree assertion needs.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 09PS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09PS)
-/

@[expose] public section

namespace DividedPowers.TateResolution

universe u v w x

/-! ### The ideals `I` and `I · A` -/

/-- The ideal `I` of `R` by which the derivation's target is reduced: the image under `q` of the
annihilator of the generator `f` of the square-zero kernel. -/
public abbrev squareZeroAnnihilator {R' : Type u} {R : Type v} [CommRing R'] [CommRing R]
    (q : R' →+* R) (f : R') : Ideal R :=
  Ideal.map q (Ideal.span {f}).annihilator

/-- Membership in `squareZeroAnnihilator q f` for the image of an element killing `f`. -/
public theorem mem_squareZeroAnnihilator {R' : Type u} {R : Type v} [CommRing R'] [CommRing R]
    {q : R' →+* R} {f r : R'} (hr : r * f = 0) :
    q r ∈ squareZeroAnnihilator q f :=
  Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ <| (Submodule.mem_annihilator_span_singleton f r).2 <| by
    rw [smul_eq_mul, hr]

/-- The submodule `I · A` of `A`, by which `A` is divided to form the derivation's domain. -/
public abbrev squareZeroAnnihilatorSMul {R' : Type u} {R : Type v} [CommRing R'] [CommRing R]
    (q : R' →+* R) (f : R') (A : Type w) [Ring A] [Algebra R A] : Submodule R A :=
  squareZeroAnnihilator q f • (⊤ : Submodule R A)

/-- A lift of the graded algebra with differential `(A, 𝒜, d)` across the surjection `q` with
square-zero principal kernel `(f)`. The operator `D` lifting `d` is *not* assumed square-zero;
its square is what produces the derivation of Tag 09PS. -/
public structure IsSquareZeroLift
    {R' : Type u} {R : Type v} {A : Type w} {B : Type x}
    [CommRing R'] [CommRing R] [Ring A] [Algebra R A] [Ring B] [Algebra R' B]
    (q : R' →+* R) (f : R')
    (𝒜 : ℕ → Submodule R A) [GradedAlgebra 𝒜] (d : A →ₗ[R] A)
    (ℬ : ℕ → Submodule R' B) [GradedAlgebra ℬ]
    (π : B →+* A) (D : B →ₗ[R'] B)
    (κ : RingHom.ker π →+ (A ⧸ squareZeroAnnihilatorSMul q f A)) : Prop where
  /-- The base map is surjective. -/
  surjective_base : Function.Surjective q
  /-- The lift is surjective. -/
  surjective : Function.Surjective π
  /-- The lift is compatible with the structure maps. -/
  map_algebraMap : ∀ r' : R', π (algebraMap R' B r') = algebraMap R A (q r')
  /-- The lift preserves the grading. -/
  map_mem_grade : ∀ (n : ℕ) (b : B), b ∈ ℬ n → π b ∈ 𝒜 n
  /-- The kernel of the lift is generated by the square-zero generator. -/
  mem_ker_iff : ∀ b : B, π b = 0 ↔ ∃ c : B, b = algebraMap R' B f * c
  /-- The lifted operator vanishes in degree zero. -/
  D_eq_zero : ∀ b : B, b ∈ ℬ 0 → D b = 0
  /-- The lifted operator lowers every positive degree by one. -/
  D_mem_grade : ∀ (n : ℕ) (b : B), b ∈ ℬ (n + 1) → D b ∈ ℬ n
  /-- The lifted operator satisfies the signed Leibniz rule on homogeneous elements. -/
  D_leibniz : ∀ (i j : ℕ) (b c : B), b ∈ ℬ i → c ∈ ℬ j →
    D (b * c) = D b * c + (-1 : R') ^ i • (b * D c)
  /-- The lifted operator is a lift of the differential. -/
  map_D : ∀ b : B, π (D b) = d (π b)
  /-- The comparison map sends `f · b` to the class of `π b`. -/
  kappa_apply : ∀ (b : B) (hb : algebraMap R' B f * b ∈ RingHom.ker π),
    κ ⟨algebraMap R' B f * b, hb⟩ = Submodule.Quotient.mk (π b)

namespace IsSquareZeroLift

section Auxiliary

variable {R' : Type u} {B : Type x} [CommRing R'] [Ring B] [Algebra R' B]

/-- The image of the square-zero generator is central, so it can be moved across a product. -/
public theorem generator_mul_comm (f : R') (b c : B) :
    b * (algebraMap R' B f * c) = algebraMap R' B f * (b * c) := by
  rw [← mul_assoc, ← Algebra.commutes, mul_assoc]

/-- Taking a homogeneous component commutes with multiplication by a scalar. -/
public theorem decompose_smul_coe (ℬ : ℕ → Submodule R' B) [GradedAlgebra ℬ]
    (r : R') (b : B) (n : ℕ) :
    ((DirectSum.decompose ℬ (r • b) n : ℬ n) : B) =
      r • ((DirectSum.decompose ℬ b n : ℬ n) : B) := by
  induction b using DirectSum.Decomposition.inductionOn ℬ with
  | zero => simp
  | @homogeneous m b =>
      rcases eq_or_ne m n with rfl | hmn
      · rw [DirectSum.decompose_of_mem_same ℬ ((ℬ m).smul_mem r b.2),
          DirectSum.decompose_of_mem_same ℬ b.2]
      · rw [DirectSum.decompose_of_mem_ne ℬ ((ℬ m).smul_mem r b.2) hmn,
          DirectSum.decompose_of_mem_ne ℬ b.2 hmn, smul_zero]
  | add b c hb hc =>
      simp only [smul_add, DirectSum.decompose_add, DirectSum.add_apply, Submodule.coe_add,
        hb, hc]

/-- A multiple of the square-zero generator which is homogeneous of degree `n` is already the
multiple of the degree-`n` component of its cofactor. -/
public theorem generator_mul_eq_of_mem_grade (ℬ : ℕ → Submodule R' B) [GradedAlgebra ℬ]
    (f : R') {β : B} {n : ℕ} (hβ : algebraMap R' B f * β ∈ ℬ n) :
    algebraMap R' B f * β =
      algebraMap R' B f * ((DirectSum.decompose ℬ β n : ℬ n) : B) := by
  have hβ' : f • β ∈ ℬ n := by rwa [← Algebra.smul_def] at hβ
  simp only [← Algebra.smul_def]
  rw [← decompose_smul_coe ℬ f β n, DirectSum.decompose_of_mem_same ℬ hβ']

end Auxiliary

variable {R' : Type u} {R : Type v} {A : Type w} {B : Type x}
  [CommRing R'] [CommRing R] [Ring A] [Algebra R A] [Ring B] [Algebra R' B]
  {q : R' →+* R} {f : R'} {𝒜 : ℕ → Submodule R A} [GradedAlgebra 𝒜] {d : A →ₗ[R] A}
  {ℬ : ℕ → Submodule R' B} [GradedAlgebra ℬ] {π : B →+* A} {D : B →ₗ[R'] B}
  {κ : RingHom.ker π →+ (A ⧸ squareZeroAnnihilatorSMul q f A)}

section Lift

variable (h : IsSquareZeroLift q f 𝒜 d ℬ π D κ)

include h

/-- Multiplication by a scalar of `R'` is carried by the lift to multiplication by its image. -/
public theorem map_smul (r : R') (b : B) : π (r • b) = q r • π b := by
  rw [Algebra.smul_def, map_mul, h.map_algebraMap, Algebra.smul_def]

/-- An element of the kernel of the lift is a multiple of the square-zero generator. -/
public theorem exists_eq_generator_mul {b : B} (hb : π b = 0) :
    ∃ c : B, b = algebraMap R' B f * c :=
  (h.mem_ker_iff b).1 hb

/-- The comparison map is determined on the whole kernel: it sends a kernel element, written as
a multiple of the square-zero generator, to the class of the image of the cofactor. -/
public theorem kappa_eq {ξ : B} (hξ : ξ ∈ RingHom.ker π) {c : B}
    (hc : ξ = algebraMap R' B f * c) :
    κ ⟨ξ, hξ⟩ = Submodule.Quotient.mk (π c) := by
  subst hc
  exact h.kappa_apply c hξ

/-- A degree-preserving surjection onto a graded algebra is surjective in every degree. -/
public theorem exists_homogeneous_preimage (n : ℕ) (x : A) (hx : x ∈ 𝒜 n) :
    ∃ b : B, b ∈ ℬ n ∧ π b = x := by
  have key : ∀ b : B, ((DirectSum.decompose 𝒜 (π b) n : 𝒜 n) : A) =
      π ((DirectSum.decompose ℬ b n : ℬ n) : B) := by
    intro b
    induction b using DirectSum.Decomposition.inductionOn ℬ with
    | zero => simp
    | @homogeneous m b =>
        rcases eq_or_ne m n with rfl | hmn
        · rw [DirectSum.decompose_of_mem_same ℬ b.2,
            DirectSum.decompose_of_mem_same 𝒜 (h.map_mem_grade m b b.2)]
        · rw [DirectSum.decompose_of_mem_ne ℬ b.2 hmn,
            DirectSum.decompose_of_mem_ne 𝒜 (h.map_mem_grade m b b.2) hmn, map_zero]
    | add b c hb hc =>
        rw [map_add, DirectSum.decompose_add, DirectSum.add_apply, Submodule.coe_add, hb, hc,
          DirectSum.decompose_add, DirectSum.add_apply, Submodule.coe_add, map_add]
  obtain ⟨b₀, hb₀⟩ := h.surjective x
  refine ⟨((DirectSum.decompose ℬ b₀ n : ℬ n) : B), (DirectSum.decompose ℬ b₀ n).2, ?_⟩
  rw [← key b₀, hb₀, DirectSum.decompose_of_mem_same 𝒜 hx]

/-- The square of the lifted operator is an unsigned derivation: the two Koszul signs of the
signed Leibniz rule cancel. -/
public theorem D_comp_D_mul (b c : B) :
    D (D (b * c)) = D (D b) * c + b * D (D c) := by
  have hom : ∀ (i j : ℕ) (b c : B), b ∈ ℬ i → c ∈ ℬ j →
      D (D (b * c)) = D (D b) * c + b * D (D c) := by
    intro i j b c hb hc
    match i, j with
    | 0, 0 =>
        have hb0 : D b = 0 := h.D_eq_zero b hb
        have hc0 : D c = 0 := h.D_eq_zero c hc
        have hbc : D (b * c) = 0 := by
          rw [h.D_leibniz 0 0 b c hb hc, hb0, hc0]
          simp
        rw [hbc, hb0, hc0]
        simp
    | 0, j + 1 =>
        have hb0 : D b = 0 := h.D_eq_zero b hb
        have hDc : D c ∈ ℬ j := h.D_mem_grade j c hc
        have hbc : D (b * c) = b * D c := by
          rw [h.D_leibniz 0 (j + 1) b c hb hc, hb0]
          simp
        rw [hbc, h.D_leibniz 0 j b (D c) hb hDc, hb0]
        simp
    | i + 1, 0 =>
        have hc0 : D c = 0 := h.D_eq_zero c hc
        have hDb : D b ∈ ℬ i := h.D_mem_grade i b hb
        have hbc : D (b * c) = D b * c := by
          rw [h.D_leibniz (i + 1) 0 b c hb hc, hc0]
          simp
        rw [hbc, h.D_leibniz i 0 (D b) c hDb hc, hc0]
        simp
    | i + 1, j + 1 =>
        have hsq : ((-1 : R') ^ (i + 1)) * ((-1 : R') ^ (i + 1)) = 1 := by
          rw [← pow_add, ← two_mul, pow_mul]
          simp
        calc D (D (b * c))
            = (D (D b) * c + ((-1 : R') ^ i) • (D b * D c)) +
                ((-1 : R') ^ (i + 1)) •
                  (D b * D c + ((-1 : R') ^ (i + 1)) • (b * D (D c))) := by
              rw [h.D_leibniz (i + 1) (j + 1) b c hb hc, map_add, D.map_smul,
                h.D_leibniz i (j + 1) (D b) c (h.D_mem_grade i b hb) hc,
                h.D_leibniz (i + 1) j b (D c) hb (h.D_mem_grade j c hc)]
          _ = D (D b) * c + b * D (D c) := by
              rw [smul_add, smul_smul, hsq, one_smul, add_assoc,
                ← add_assoc (((-1 : R') ^ i) • (D b * D c)), ← add_smul, pow_succ]
              simp
  induction b using DirectSum.Decomposition.inductionOn ℬ with
  | zero => simp
  | @homogeneous i b =>
      induction c using DirectSum.Decomposition.inductionOn ℬ with
      | zero => simp
      | @homogeneous j c => exact hom i j b c b.2 c.2
      | add c c' hc hc' =>
          simp only [mul_add, map_add, hc, hc']
          abel
  | add b b' hb hb' =>
      simp only [add_mul, map_add, hb, hb']
      abel

end Lift

section Differential

variable [IsDifferentialGradedAlgebra 𝒜 d] (h : IsSquareZeroLift q f 𝒜 d ℬ π D κ)

include h

/-- The square of the lifted operator takes values in the kernel of the lift, because the
differential it lifts is square-zero. -/
public theorem map_D_comp_D (b : B) : π (D (D b)) = 0 := by
  rw [h.map_D, h.map_D]
  exact IsDifferentialGradedAlgebra.d_sq_zero (𝒜 := 𝒜) (d := d) (π b)

/-- The square of the lifted operator, compared into `A/IA`. This is the derivation of
Tag 09PS before it is descended along the lift. -/
public noncomputable def preDerivation (b : B) : A ⧸ squareZeroAnnihilatorSMul q f A :=
  κ ⟨D (D b), h.map_D_comp_D b⟩

/-- The comparison of the square of the lifted operator is the value of `κ` on it. -/
public theorem preDerivation_eq_kappa (b : B) (hb : D (D b) ∈ RingHom.ker π) :
    h.preDerivation b = κ ⟨D (D b), hb⟩ := rfl

/-- The comparison of the square of the lifted operator is additive. -/
public theorem preDerivation_add (b c : B) :
    h.preDerivation (b + c) = h.preDerivation b + h.preDerivation c := by
  rw [h.preDerivation_eq_kappa (b + c) (h.map_D_comp_D _),
    h.preDerivation_eq_kappa b (h.map_D_comp_D _),
    h.preDerivation_eq_kappa c (h.map_D_comp_D _), ← map_add]
  congr 1
  apply Subtype.ext
  simp

/-- The comparison of the square of the lifted operator, read off a presentation of that square
as a multiple of the square-zero generator. -/
public theorem preDerivation_eq {b β : B} (hβ : D (D b) = algebraMap R' B f * β) :
    h.preDerivation b = Submodule.Quotient.mk (π β) :=
  h.kappa_eq (h.map_D_comp_D b) hβ

/-- The comparison of the square of the lifted operator is semilinear over `q`. -/
public theorem preDerivation_smul (r : R') (b : B) :
    h.preDerivation (r • b) = q r • h.preDerivation b := by
  obtain ⟨β, hβ⟩ := h.exists_eq_generator_mul (h.map_D_comp_D b)
  have hr : D (D (r • b)) = algebraMap R' B f * (r • β) := by
    rw [D.map_smul, D.map_smul, hβ]
    exact (mul_smul_comm r _ β).symm
  rw [h.preDerivation_eq hr, h.preDerivation_eq hβ, h.map_smul, Submodule.Quotient.mk_smul]

/-- Two elements with the same image under the lift have the same comparison. -/
public theorem preDerivation_congr {b c : B} (hbc : π b = π c) :
    h.preDerivation b = h.preDerivation c := by
  have hker : π (b - c) = 0 := by rw [map_sub, hbc, sub_self]
  obtain ⟨e, he⟩ := h.exists_eq_generator_mul hker
  have hval : D (D (b - c)) = algebraMap R' B f * D (D e) := by
    rw [he, ← Algebra.smul_def, D.map_smul, D.map_smul, Algebra.smul_def]
  have hzero : h.preDerivation (b - c) = 0 := by
    rw [h.preDerivation_eq hval, h.map_D, h.map_D,
      IsDifferentialGradedAlgebra.d_sq_zero (𝒜 := 𝒜) (d := d) (π e)]
    simp
  have hsub : h.preDerivation (b - c) + h.preDerivation c = h.preDerivation b := by
    rw [← h.preDerivation_add, sub_add_cancel]
  rw [← hsub, hzero, zero_add]

/-- The comparison of the square of the lifted operator vanishes on elements whose image lies in
`I · A`. -/
public theorem preDerivation_eq_zero_of_map_mem {b : B}
    (hb : π b ∈ squareZeroAnnihilatorSMul q f A) :
    h.preDerivation b = 0 := by
  have main : ∀ x : A, x ∈ squareZeroAnnihilatorSMul q f A →
      ∃ c : B, π c = x ∧ h.preDerivation c = 0 := by
    intro x hx
    refine Submodule.smul_induction_on hx ?_ ?_
    · intro r hr a _
      obtain ⟨s, hs, hqs⟩ := (Ideal.mem_map_iff_of_surjective q h.surjective_base).1 hr
      obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := h.surjective a
      have hsf : s * f = 0 := by
        have hsmul := Submodule.mem_annihilator.1 hs f (Ideal.mem_span_singleton_self f)
        simpa [smul_eq_mul] using hsmul
      refine ⟨s • c, by rw [h.map_smul, hqs, hc], ?_⟩
      obtain ⟨β, hβ⟩ := h.exists_eq_generator_mul (h.map_D_comp_D c)
      have hval : D (D (s • c)) = algebraMap R' B f * 0 := by
        rw [D.map_smul, D.map_smul, hβ, Algebra.smul_def, ← mul_assoc, ← map_mul, hsf, map_zero,
          zero_mul, mul_zero]
      rw [h.preDerivation_eq hval, map_zero]
      simp
    · rintro x y ⟨c, hc, hc0⟩ ⟨e, he, he0⟩
      exact ⟨c + e, by rw [map_add, hc, he], by rw [h.preDerivation_add, hc0, he0, add_zero]⟩
  obtain ⟨c, hc, hc0⟩ := main (π b) hb
  rw [h.preDerivation_congr hc.symm, hc0]

/-- The comparison of the square of the lifted operator, transported to `A` along a
set-theoretic section of the lift. -/
public noncomputable def liftedPreDerivation :
    A →ₗ[R] A ⧸ squareZeroAnnihilatorSMul q f A where
  toFun a := h.preDerivation (Function.surjInv h.surjective a)
  map_add' x y := by
    obtain ⟨b, hb⟩ := h.surjective x
    obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := h.surjective y
    rw [show h.preDerivation (Function.surjInv h.surjective (x + y)) = h.preDerivation (b + c) from
        h.preDerivation_congr (by rw [Function.surjInv_eq h.surjective, map_add, hb, hc]),
      show h.preDerivation (Function.surjInv h.surjective x) = h.preDerivation b from
        h.preDerivation_congr (by rw [Function.surjInv_eq h.surjective, hb]),
      show h.preDerivation (Function.surjInv h.surjective y) = h.preDerivation c from
        h.preDerivation_congr (by rw [Function.surjInv_eq h.surjective, hc]),
      h.preDerivation_add]
  map_smul' r x := by
    obtain ⟨r', hr'⟩ := h.surjective_base r
    obtain ⟨b, hb⟩ := h.surjective x
    rw [RingHom.id_apply,
      show h.preDerivation (Function.surjInv h.surjective (r • x)) =
          h.preDerivation (r' • b) from
        h.preDerivation_congr (by rw [Function.surjInv_eq h.surjective, h.map_smul, hr', hb]),
      show h.preDerivation (Function.surjInv h.surjective x) = h.preDerivation b from
        h.preDerivation_congr (by rw [Function.surjInv_eq h.surjective, hb]),
      h.preDerivation_smul, hr']

/-- The transported comparison, computed on an image under the lift. -/
public theorem liftedPreDerivation_map (b : B) :
    h.liftedPreDerivation (π b) = h.preDerivation b :=
  h.preDerivation_congr (by rw [Function.surjInv_eq h.surjective])

/-- The derivation `θ` of Tag 09PS: the square of the lifted operator, compared into `A/IA` and
descended along the lift. -/
public noncomputable def derivation :
    (A ⧸ squareZeroAnnihilatorSMul q f A) →ₗ[R] (A ⧸ squareZeroAnnihilatorSMul q f A) :=
  Submodule.liftQ _ h.liftedPreDerivation (by
    intro x hx
    obtain ⟨b, hb⟩ := h.surjective x
    rw [LinearMap.mem_ker, ← hb, h.liftedPreDerivation_map]
    exact h.preDerivation_eq_zero_of_map_mem (hb ▸ hx))

/-- The derivation evaluated on a class in the image of the lift. -/
public theorem derivation_mk_map (b : B) :
    h.derivation (Submodule.Quotient.mk (π b)) = h.preDerivation b := by
  rw [derivation, Submodule.liftQ_apply, h.liftedPreDerivation_map]

/-- The derivation is the comparison of the square of the lifted operator; this determines
`θ`. -/
public theorem derivation_apply (b : B) (hb : D (D b) ∈ RingHom.ker π) :
    h.derivation (Submodule.Quotient.mk (π b)) = κ ⟨D (D b), hb⟩ := by
  rw [h.derivation_mk_map, h.preDerivation_eq_kappa b hb]

/-- The derivation evaluated through a presentation of the square of the lifted operator as a
multiple of the square-zero generator. -/
public theorem derivation_mk_map_eq {b β : B} (hβ : D (D b) = algebraMap R' B f * β) :
    h.derivation (Submodule.Quotient.mk (π b)) = Submodule.Quotient.mk (π β) := by
  rw [h.derivation_mk_map, h.preDerivation_eq hβ]

/-- The derivation satisfies the Leibniz rule, stated through lifts of its two values. -/
public theorem derivation_leibniz (x y : A) :
    ∃ u v : A,
      h.derivation (Submodule.Quotient.mk x) = Submodule.Quotient.mk u ∧
      h.derivation (Submodule.Quotient.mk y) = Submodule.Quotient.mk v ∧
      h.derivation (Submodule.Quotient.mk (x * y)) =
        Submodule.Quotient.mk (u * y + x * v) := by
  obtain ⟨b, hb⟩ := h.surjective x
  obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := h.surjective y
  obtain ⟨β, hβ⟩ := h.exists_eq_generator_mul (h.map_D_comp_D b)
  obtain ⟨γ, hγ⟩ := h.exists_eq_generator_mul (h.map_D_comp_D c)
  refine ⟨π β, π γ, ?_, ?_, ?_⟩
  · rw [← hb, h.derivation_mk_map_eq hβ]
  · rw [← hc, h.derivation_mk_map_eq hγ]
  · have hprod : D (D (b * c)) = algebraMap R' B f * (β * c + b * γ) := by
      rw [h.D_comp_D_mul, hβ, hγ, mul_add, mul_assoc, generator_mul_comm f b γ]
    rw [← hb, ← hc, ← map_mul, h.derivation_mk_map_eq hprod, map_add, map_mul, map_mul]

/-- The derivation lowers degrees by two. -/
public theorem derivation_mem_grade (n : ℕ) (x : A) (hx : x ∈ 𝒜 (n + 2)) :
    ∃ y : A, y ∈ 𝒜 n ∧
      h.derivation (Submodule.Quotient.mk x) = Submodule.Quotient.mk y := by
  obtain ⟨b, hbmem, hb⟩ := h.exists_homogeneous_preimage (n + 2) x hx
  have hDD : D (D b) ∈ ℬ n :=
    h.D_mem_grade n (D b) (h.D_mem_grade (n + 1) b hbmem)
  obtain ⟨β, hβ⟩ := h.exists_eq_generator_mul (h.map_D_comp_D b)
  rw [hβ] at hDD
  refine ⟨π ((DirectSum.decompose ℬ β n : ℬ n) : B),
    h.map_mem_grade n _ (DirectSum.decompose ℬ β n).2, ?_⟩
  rw [← hb, h.derivation_mk_map_eq (hβ.trans (generator_mul_eq_of_mem_grade ℬ f hDD))]

/-- The derivation vanishes in degree zero. -/
public theorem derivation_eq_zero_of_mem_grade_zero (x : A) (hx : x ∈ 𝒜 0) :
    h.derivation (Submodule.Quotient.mk x) = 0 := by
  obtain ⟨b, hbmem, hb⟩ := h.exists_homogeneous_preimage 0 x hx
  have hval : D (D b) = algebraMap R' B f * 0 := by
    rw [h.D_eq_zero b hbmem, map_zero, mul_zero]
  rw [← hb, h.derivation_mk_map_eq hval, map_zero]
  simp

/-- The derivation vanishes in degree one. -/
public theorem derivation_eq_zero_of_mem_grade_one (x : A) (hx : x ∈ 𝒜 1) :
    h.derivation (Submodule.Quotient.mk x) = 0 := by
  obtain ⟨b, hbmem, hb⟩ := h.exists_homogeneous_preimage 1 x hx
  have hval : D (D b) = algebraMap R' B f * 0 := by
    rw [h.D_eq_zero (D b) (h.D_mem_grade 0 b hbmem), mul_zero]
  rw [← hb, h.derivation_mk_map_eq hval, map_zero]
  simp

end Differential

end IsSquareZeroLift

/-- A square-zero lift which additionally carries divided powers: the lift is a morphism of
divided powers, and the lifted operator obeys the divided-power Leibniz rule. These conditions
play no part in the four properties of the derivation, but they are what the Gulliksen argument
of Tag 09PU runs on: that argument differentiates `δ.dpow m b` for a lift `b` of a degree-two
class and transports the result back along `π`. -/
public structure IsDividedPowerSquareZeroLift
    {R' : Type u} {R : Type v} {A : Type w} {B : Type x}
    [CommRing R'] [CommRing R] [Ring A] [Algebra R A] [Ring B] [Algebra R' B]
    (q : R' →+* R) (f : R')
    (𝒜 : ℕ → Submodule R A) [GradedAlgebra 𝒜] [IsStrictlyGradedComm 𝒜]
    (γ : DividedPowerStructure 𝒜) (d : A →ₗ[R] A)
    (ℬ : ℕ → Submodule R' B) [GradedAlgebra ℬ] [IsStrictlyGradedComm ℬ]
    (δ : DividedPowerStructure ℬ)
    (π : B →+* A) (D : B →ₗ[R'] B)
    (κ : RingHom.ker π →+ (A ⧸ squareZeroAnnihilatorSMul q f A))
    : Prop extends IsSquareZeroLift q f 𝒜 d ℬ π D κ where
  /-- The lift is a morphism of divided powers. -/
  map_dpow : ∀ (n : ℕ) (b : B), b ∈ positiveEvenPart ℬ →
    π (δ.dpow n b) = γ.dpow n (π b)
  /-- The lifted operator obeys the divided-power Leibniz rule. -/
  D_dpow : ∀ (n : ℕ) (b : B), n ≠ 0 → b ∈ positiveEvenPart ℬ →
    D (δ.dpow n b) = D b * δ.dpow (n - 1) b

/-! ### The existential form of the lift

The same descent, stated as an existence result over the raw data of a lift rather than over
the `IsSquareZeroLift` predicate. It needs no comparison map `κ` supplied in advance, and
constructs one instead.
-/

/-- An additive map that kills the kernel of a surjective additive map factors through it. -/
public theorem exists_addMonoidHom_comp_of_surjective
    {M : Type u} {N : Type v} {P : Type w}
    [AddCommGroup M] [AddCommGroup N] [AddCommGroup P]
    (p : M →+ N) (hp : Function.Surjective p) (g : M →+ P)
    (hg : ∀ m : M, p m = 0 → g m = 0) :
    ∃ G : N →+ P, ∀ m : M, G (p m) = g m := by
  classical
  have key : ∀ (m : M) (n : N), p m = n → g (Function.surjInv hp n) = g m := by
    intro m n hmn
    have h0 : p (Function.surjInv hp n - m) = 0 := by
      rw [map_sub, Function.surjInv_eq hp n, hmn, sub_self]
    have h1 := hg _ h0
    rw [map_sub, sub_eq_zero] at h1
    exact h1
  refine ⟨{ toFun := fun n => g (Function.surjInv hp n)
            map_zero' := ?_
            map_add' := ?_ }, ?_⟩
  · rw [key 0 0 (map_zero p), map_zero]
  · intro n₁ n₂
    obtain ⟨m₁, hm₁⟩ := hp n₁
    obtain ⟨m₂, hm₂⟩ := hp n₂
    show g (Function.surjInv hp (n₁ + n₂)) =
      g (Function.surjInv hp n₁) + g (Function.surjInv hp n₂)
    rw [key m₁ n₁ hm₁, key m₂ n₂ hm₂,
      key (m₁ + m₂) (n₁ + n₂) (by rw [map_add, hm₁, hm₂]), map_add]
  · intro m
    exact key m (p m) rfl

/-- In a free module, an element annihilated by `r` lies in the submodule cut out by the
annihilator of `r`: its coordinates in any basis all annihilate `r`. -/
public theorem mem_annihilator_smul_top_of_smul_eq_zero
    {R : Type u} {M : Type v} [CommRing R] [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M] [Module.Free R M]
    (r : R) (x : M) (hx : r • x = 0) :
    x ∈ (Ideal.span {r}).annihilator • (⊤ : Submodule R M) := by
  classical
  let b := Module.Free.chooseBasis R M
  have hzero : r • b.repr x = 0 := by rw [← map_smul, hx, map_zero]
  have hcoord : ∀ i, b.repr x i ∈ (Ideal.span {r}).annihilator := by
    intro i
    have hi : r * b.repr x i = 0 := by
      have h := congrArg (fun l : _ →₀ R => l i) hzero
      simpa using h
    rw [Submodule.mem_annihilator]
    intro n hn
    obtain ⟨c, rfl⟩ := Ideal.mem_span_singleton'.mp hn
    have : b.repr x i • (c * r) = c * (r * b.repr x i) := by
      rw [smul_eq_mul]; ring
    rw [this, hi, mul_zero]
  rw [← b.linearCombination_repr x, Finsupp.linearCombination_apply, Finsupp.sum]
  refine Submodule.sum_mem _ fun i _ => ?_
  exact Submodule.smul_mem_smul (hcoord i) Submodule.mem_top

/-- An additive map carrying every homogeneous piece into the piece of the same degree commutes
with taking homogeneous components. -/
public theorem coe_decompose_addMonoidHom
    {R' : Type u} {R : Type v} {A : Type w} {B : Type x}
    [CommRing R'] [CommRing R] [Ring A] [Algebra R A] [Ring B] [Algebra R' B]
    (𝒜 : ℕ → Submodule R A) [GradedAlgebra 𝒜]
    (ℬ : ℕ → Submodule R' B) [GradedAlgebra ℬ]
    (g : B →+ A) (hg : ∀ (n : ℕ) (b : B), b ∈ ℬ n → g b ∈ 𝒜 n) (n : ℕ) (b : B) :
    (DirectSum.decompose 𝒜 (g b) n : A) = g (DirectSum.decompose ℬ b n : B) := by
  classical
  refine DirectSum.Decomposition.inductionOn ℬ (zero := ?_) (homogeneous := ?_)
    (add := ?_) b
  · simp
  · intro i y
    by_cases hin : i = n
    · subst hin
      rw [DirectSum.decompose_of_mem_same ℬ y.2,
        DirectSum.decompose_of_mem_same 𝒜 (hg i (y : B) y.2)]
    · rw [DirectSum.decompose_of_mem_ne ℬ y.2 hin,
        DirectSum.decompose_of_mem_ne 𝒜 (hg i (y : B) y.2) hin]
      exact (map_zero g).symm
  · intro y z hy hz
    rw [map_add, DirectSum.decompose_add, DirectSum.decompose_add, DirectSum.add_apply,
      DirectSum.add_apply, Submodule.coe_add, Submodule.coe_add, hy, hz, map_add]

/-! ### Ideals generated by central scalars -/

section CentralIdeals

variable {R : Type u} {A : Type v} [CommRing R] [Ring A] [Algebra R A]

/-- An ideal generated by the image of a central scalar ideal is two-sided. -/
public instance (priority := low) isTwoSided_map_algebraMap (I : Ideal R) :
    (I.map (algebraMap R A)).IsTwoSided := by
  refine ⟨fun {a} b ha => ?_⟩
  rw [Ideal.map, Ideal.span] at ha ⊢
  induction ha using Submodule.span_induction with
  | mem x hx =>
      obtain ⟨r, hr, rfl⟩ := hx
      rw [Algebra.commutes]
      exact Ideal.mul_mem_left _ _ (Submodule.subset_span ⟨r, hr, rfl⟩)
  | zero => simp
  | add x y _ _ hx hy => rw [add_mul]; exact Submodule.add_mem _ hx hy
  | smul c x _ hx => rw [smul_eq_mul, mul_assoc]; exact Ideal.mul_mem_left _ _ hx

/-- The submodule `I • A` absorbs multiplication by `A`. -/
public theorem mul_mem_smul_top (I : Ideal R) (c : A) {x : A}
    (hx : x ∈ I • (⊤ : Submodule R A)) : c * x ∈ I • (⊤ : Submodule R A) := by
  refine Submodule.smul_induction_on hx ?_ ?_
  · intro r hr z _
    rw [mul_smul_comm]
    exact Submodule.smul_mem_smul hr Submodule.mem_top
  · intro x y hx hy
    rw [mul_add]
    exact Submodule.add_mem _ hx hy

/-- The ideal of `A` generated by a central scalar ideal `I` is, as an `R`-submodule, `I • A`. -/
public theorem restrictScalars_map_algebraMap (I : Ideal R) :
    (I.map (algebraMap R A)).restrictScalars R = I • (⊤ : Submodule R A) := by
  refine le_antisymm (fun a ha => ?_) ?_
  · rw [Submodule.restrictScalars_mem, Ideal.map, Ideal.span] at ha
    induction ha using Submodule.span_induction with
    | mem x hx =>
        obtain ⟨r, hr, rfl⟩ := hx
        have hr1 : algebraMap R A r = r • (1 : A) := by rw [Algebra.smul_def, mul_one]
        rw [hr1]
        exact Submodule.smul_mem_smul hr Submodule.mem_top
    | zero => simp
    | add x y _ _ hx hy => exact Submodule.add_mem _ hx hy
    | smul c x _ hx => rw [smul_eq_mul]; exact mul_mem_smul_top I c hx
  · rw [Submodule.smul_le]
    intro r hr a _
    rw [Submodule.restrictScalars_mem, Algebra.smul_def]
    exact Ideal.mul_mem_right _ _ (Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ hr)

/-- Scalar multiplication on the quotient by an ideal generated by central scalars. -/
public theorem smul_mk_eq (I : Ideal R) (r : R) (y : A) :
    r • (Ideal.Quotient.mk (I.map (algebraMap R A)) y)
      = Ideal.Quotient.mk _ (algebraMap R A r * y) := by
  rw [Algebra.smul_def, ← Ideal.Quotient.mk_algebraMap (R₁ := R), ← map_mul]

end CentralIdeals

/-! ### Graded preliminaries -/

section Graded

variable {R' : Type u} {B : Type w} [CommRing R'] [Ring B] [Algebra R' B]
  (ℬ : ℕ → Submodule R' B) [GradedAlgebra ℬ]

/-- The image of a scalar in a graded algebra has degree zero. -/
public theorem algebraMap_mem_grade_zero (f : R') : algebraMap R' B f ∈ ℬ 0 :=
  SetLike.algebraMap_mem_graded ℬ f

/-- Multiplication by a degree-zero element commutes with the homogeneous projections. -/
public theorem proj_mul_of_mem_grade_zero {z : B} (hz : z ∈ ℬ 0) (c : B) (n : ℕ) :
    GradedRing.proj ℬ n (z * c) = z * GradedRing.proj ℬ n c := by
  classical
  have hc : c ∈ ⨆ i, ℬ i := by
    rw [(DirectSum.Decomposition.isInternal ℬ).submodule_iSup_eq_top]; trivial
  induction hc using Submodule.iSup_induction' with
  | mem i w hw =>
      have hzw : z * w ∈ ℬ i := by
        have hmul := SetLike.GradedMul.mul_mem hz hw
        rwa [zero_add] at hmul
      by_cases hin : i = n
      · subst hin
        rw [GradedRing.proj_apply, DirectSum.decompose_of_mem_same ℬ hzw,
          GradedRing.proj_apply, DirectSum.decompose_of_mem_same ℬ hw]
      · rw [GradedRing.proj_apply, DirectSum.decompose_of_mem_ne ℬ hzw hin,
          GradedRing.proj_apply, DirectSum.decompose_of_mem_ne ℬ hw hin, mul_zero]
  | zero => simp
  | add x y _ _ ihx ihy => rw [mul_add, map_add, ihx, ihy, map_add, mul_add]

end Graded

/-! ### The derivation from an unbundled lift of the differential -/

/-- **The derivation of a principal square-zero extension, given a lift of the differential.**

Let `q : R' → R` be a surjection with kernel generated by a square-zero element `f`, let `A` be a
graded `R`-algebra with `d ∘ d = 0`, and let `I` be the image in `R` of the annihilator of `f`.
Suppose the differential lifts across `q`: there is a graded `R'`-algebra `B` in which an
element killed by `f` lies in `ann (f) • ⊤` — as happens when `B` is free over `R'`, by
`mem_annihilator_smul_top_of_smul_eq_zero` — a grading-preserving surjection `π : B → A`
whose kernel is `f B`, and an
`R'`-linear `D` on `B` which vanishes in degree zero, lowers degree by one, satisfies the signed
Leibniz rule, and satisfies `π ∘ D = d ∘ π`.

Then multiplication by `f` identifies `A / I A` with the kernel of `π`, by a map `κ`, and
`D ∘ D` descends to a derivation `θ` of degree minus two on `A / I A`. -/
public theorem exists_derivation_of_differentialLift
    {R' : Type u} {R : Type v} {A : Type w} {B : Type x}
    [CommRing R'] [CommRing R] [Ring A] [Algebra R A] [Ring B] [Algebra R' B]
    (q : R' →+* R) (hq : Function.Surjective q)
    (f : R') (hker : RingHom.ker q = Ideal.span {f})
    (_hsq : (RingHom.ker q) ^ 2 = ⊥)
    (𝒜 : ℕ → Submodule R A) [GradedAlgebra 𝒜]
    (d : A →ₗ[R] A) (hdsq : ∀ a : A, d (d a) = 0)
    (ℬ : ℕ → Submodule R' B) [GradedAlgebra ℬ]
    (π : B →+* A) (hπ : Function.Surjective π) (D : B →ₗ[R'] B)
    (hfann : ∀ b : B, f • b = 0 → b ∈ (Ideal.span {f}).annihilator • (⊤ : Submodule R' B))
    (hπalg : ∀ r' : R', π (algebraMap R' B r') = algebraMap R A (q r'))
    (hπgrade : ∀ (n : ℕ) (b : B), b ∈ ℬ n → π b ∈ 𝒜 n)
    (hπker : ∀ b : B, π b = 0 ↔ ∃ c : B, b = algebraMap R' B f * c)
    (hD0 : ∀ b : B, b ∈ ℬ 0 → D b = 0)
    (hDgrade : ∀ (n : ℕ) (b : B), b ∈ ℬ (n + 1) → D b ∈ ℬ n)
    (hDleibniz : ∀ (i j : ℕ) (b c : B), b ∈ ℬ i → c ∈ ℬ j →
      D (b * c) = D b * c + (-1 : R') ^ i • (b * D c))
    (hDπ : ∀ b : B, π (D b) = d (π b)) :
    let I : Ideal R := Ideal.map q (Ideal.span {f}).annihilator
    let J : Submodule R A := I • ⊤
    ∃ (θ : (A ⧸ J) →ₗ[R] (A ⧸ J)) (κ : RingHom.ker π →+ (A ⧸ J)),
      (∀ (b : B) (hb : algebraMap R' B f * b ∈ RingHom.ker π),
        κ ⟨algebraMap R' B f * b, hb⟩ = Submodule.Quotient.mk (π b)) ∧
      (∀ b : B, ∃ hb : D (D b) ∈ RingHom.ker π,
        θ (Submodule.Quotient.mk (π b)) = κ ⟨D (D b), hb⟩) ∧
      (∀ x y : A, ∃ u v : A,
        θ (Submodule.Quotient.mk x) = Submodule.Quotient.mk u ∧
        θ (Submodule.Quotient.mk y) = Submodule.Quotient.mk v ∧
        θ (Submodule.Quotient.mk (x * y)) =
          Submodule.Quotient.mk (u * y + x * v)) ∧
      (∀ (n : ℕ) (x : A), x ∈ 𝒜 (n + 2) →
        ∃ y : A, y ∈ 𝒜 n ∧
          θ (Submodule.Quotient.mk x) = Submodule.Quotient.mk y) ∧
      (∀ x : A, x ∈ 𝒜 0 → θ (Submodule.Quotient.mk x) = 0) ∧
      (∀ x : A, x ∈ 𝒜 1 → θ (Submodule.Quotient.mk x) = 0) := by
  classical
  intro I J
  have hqf : q f = 0 := by
    rw [← RingHom.mem_ker, hker]
    exact Ideal.mem_span_singleton_self f
  have hmulF_mem : ∀ b : B, algebraMap R' B f * b ∈ RingHom.ker π := fun b => by
    rw [RingHom.mem_ker, map_mul, hπalg, hqf, map_zero, zero_mul]
  -- The annihilator hypothesis is used exactly here: an element killed by `f` has class zero
  -- in `A / I A`.
  have hann : ∀ b : B, algebraMap R' B f * b = 0 → Submodule.Quotient.mk (π b) = (0 : A ⧸ J) := by
    intro b hb
    rw [Submodule.Quotient.mk_eq_zero]
    refine Submodule.smul_induction_on (p := fun y => π y ∈ J) (hfann b (by rwa [Algebra.smul_def]))
      ?_ ?_
    · intro r hr y _
      rw [Algebra.smul_def, map_mul, hπalg, ← Algebra.smul_def]
      exact Submodule.smul_mem_smul (Ideal.mem_map_of_mem q hr) Submodule.mem_top
    · intro y z hy hz
      rw [map_add]
      exact Submodule.add_mem _ hy hz
  -- The identification `κ` of `f B` with `A / I A`.
  let mulF : B →+ RingHom.ker π :=
    { toFun := fun b => ⟨algebraMap R' B f * b, hmulF_mem b⟩
      map_zero' := by apply Subtype.ext; simp
      map_add' := fun b c => by apply Subtype.ext; simp [mul_add] }
  have hmulF_surj : Function.Surjective mulF := by
    intro y
    obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := (hπker (y : B)).mp (RingHom.mem_ker.mp y.2)
    exact ⟨c, Subtype.ext hc.symm⟩
  obtain ⟨κ, hκ⟩ := exists_addMonoidHom_comp_of_surjective mulF hmulF_surj
    ((J.mkQ.toAddMonoidHom).comp (π : B →+* A).toAddMonoidHom)
    (fun b hb => hann b (congrArg Subtype.val hb))
  have h : IsSquareZeroLift q f 𝒜 d ℬ π D κ :=
    ⟨hq, hπ, hπalg, hπgrade, hπker, hD0, hDgrade, hDleibniz, hDπ, fun b _ => hκ b⟩
  -- The differential of `A` is recovered from that of `B`, so the bundled derivation applies.
  have : IsDifferentialGradedAlgebra 𝒜 d :=
    { d_grade_zero := fun {x} hx => by
        obtain ⟨b, hb, rfl⟩ := h.exists_homogeneous_preimage 0 x hx
        rw [← hDπ, hD0 b hb, map_zero]
      d_mem := fun {n x} hx => by
        obtain ⟨b, hb, rfl⟩ := h.exists_homogeneous_preimage _ x hx
        rw [← hDπ]
        exact hπgrade n _ (hDgrade n b hb)
      d_sq_zero := hdsq
      leibniz := fun {i j x y} hx hy => by
        obtain ⟨b, hb, rfl⟩ := h.exists_homogeneous_preimage i x hx
        obtain ⟨c, hc, rfl⟩ := h.exists_homogeneous_preimage j y hy
        rw [← map_mul, ← hDπ, hDleibniz i j b c hb hc, map_add, h.map_smul, map_pow, map_neg,
          map_one, map_mul, map_mul, hDπ, hDπ] }
  exact ⟨h.derivation, κ, h.kappa_apply, fun b => ⟨h.map_D_comp_D b, h.derivation_apply b _⟩,
    h.derivation_leibniz, h.derivation_mem_grade, h.derivation_eq_zero_of_mem_grade_zero,
    h.derivation_eq_zero_of_mem_grade_one⟩

end DividedPowers.TateResolution
